hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6931","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Nu'aym, on the authority of his father, said: Ma'iz Ibn Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so stand up. In the Book of God, until he came four times, and said: “Take him and stone him.” When the stones touched him, he winced and became stronger, so Abdul came out. God was among his desert, so he threw at him with the back of a donkey, which struck him, and the people threw at him until they killed him, so his escape was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Will you not leave him alone? Perhaps he will repent and God will turn to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6932","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim informed me, on the authority of Abu Uthman. Ibn Nasr Al-Sulami, on the authority of his father, said: I was among those who stoned a goat, and when stones covered it, he said: Return me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We denied that, so I went to Asim bin Omar bin Qatada and mentioned that to him, and he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad said to me: I have This reached me, so I denied it, so I went to Jabir bin Abdullah and said to him: The people mentioned something about Ma’iz saying: Return me. So I denied him, and he said: I was among those who stoned him. When he found that he was touching stones, he said: Return me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. My people deceived me. They said: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for he will not kill you. We did not give up on him until we killed him. Then when We mentioned that to him, and he said: Don’t you leave him until I look into his matter? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6933","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim told me, On the authority of Abu al-Haytham ibn Dahr al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, he said: I was among those who stoned him, and when he found that he had touched the stones, he was greatly alarmed. So we mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “So, will you leave him alone?” Muhammad said: So I remembered that from his hadith when I heard it: “Did you not abandon it” to Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, and he said to me: Hassan bin Muhammad told me. Ibn Ali Ibn Abi Talib, he said: This was narrated to me from the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Have you not abandoned it?” by Ma’iz Ibn Malik, who You wanted from the men of Aslam whom I do not accuse, and I did not know the basis of the hadith, so I went to Jabir bin Abdullah and said: The men of Aslam are speaking to me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them when they mentioned a goat being startled by stones when they hit it: “So, will you not leave it?” and what He accused the people, and I did not know the hadith. He said: O my nephew, I am the most knowledgeable of the people about this hadith. I was among those who stoned the man. When we brought him out, we stoned him, and he found himself touching the stones. He shouted at us: O my people, return me to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Indeed, my people killed me, deceived me from myself, and told me that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not my killer. So he did not We separated from him until we killed him. Then when we returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “So will you not leave the man and bring him to me?” So that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would be steadfast in it. As for leaving out a punishment, then no. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This chain of narration is better than the one before it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6934","Ahmad ibn Sa`id al-Marwazi al-Rabbati told us, he said: Ya`qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq told me Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham ibn Nasr ibn Dahr al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, said: Ma’iz ibn Malik, a man from among us, came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he mentioned a word that means: So he admitted to himself committing adultery, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to stone him. So we took him out to Harrat Banu Niyar, and stoned him. When he found that he was touching the stones, he was greatly alarmed. When we finished with him, we returned to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we mentioned his anxiety to him, and he said: “So, will you leave him alone?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6935","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad, he is ibn Abd al-Warith, narrated to me, he said: Zakaria ibn Sulaym told us, he said: I heard a man, Amr bin Othman narrates that he heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra say: My father told me that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted a grey-haired mule, when a woman came to him and said, “She has committed a sin, so go ahead of her.” He said to her, “Go back and take cover.” God, so she pleaded with him three times, each one of them saying to her: Go back, and take cover with God’s cover. So she called him to him, unless the punishment was imposed on her, so he said : You stay until you give birth to what is in your belly. So she went, then she came and said: I have given birth to a boy. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took care of him. He greeted her, then said to her: Go until you are purified. So she went, then came back and said: She has been purified. So he sent women with her. So they ascertained that she had been purified, then they came and bore witness to him that she had been purified, so he ordered Hufarah to go to her then, and then he came and the Muslims With him, he took a pebble like a chickpea and threw it with it, then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the Muslims: Throw it, and fear its face. He prayed over her and said: If her repentance were divided among the people of Hijaz, it would be enough for them. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told me, he said: I am Zakaria Abu Imran, he said: I heard a sheikh with Saeed bin Amr bin Othman said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra told us, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing. . . So he mentioned something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6936","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that A man committed adultery with a woman. “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the punishment be flogged. Then he was told that he was married, so he ordered that he be flogged, and he was stoned.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know that anyone narrated this hadith other than Ibn Wahb. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6937","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abu Asim, who is the nobleman, who said: I am Ibn Jurayj. He said: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah, he said about “A married man committed adultery, and he was not aware of his chastity until he was flogged, then he learned of his chastity, and he said: He will be stoned,” Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: This is correct, and the one before it was wrong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6938","Ziyad bin Ayyub bin Dalawayh told me, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Jews came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. A man from among them and a woman had committed adultery. He said: “What do you find in your book?” They said: “We will make their faces black, and they will be ashamed.” He said: You lied, for in it is stoning. So go to the Torah, and recite it if you are truthful. So they brought the Torah, and they brought a one-eyed reciter of theirs, so he recited. Until, when he reached one of the places, he placed his hand on it, and it was said to him: Raise your hand. So he raised it, and it was waving. They said: O Muhammad, “It involves stoning, but we were keeping it secret among ourselves, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to be done.” That's it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6939","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told me from his book. He said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us. He said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar said that he told him that when they were brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “What do you find in your book? They said: We do not find stoning.” He said Abdullah bin Salam: They lied, stoning is in their book, so it was said: Bring the Torah, and recite it if you are truthful. So they brought the Torah. Their reciter came and placed his palm on the place of stoning, so he began to read everything other than that, and Abdullah bin Salam said to him: Remove your palm. Then he saw stoning, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to be stoned, so they were stoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6940","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Musa told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar. The Jews came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man and a woman who had committed adultery. Who among you? He said: Let us strike them. He said: What do you find in the Torah? They said: We do not find anything in it. Abdullah bin Salam said: They lied about the Torah. Stoning, then bring the Torah, and recite it if you are truthful. So they brought the Torah, and the teacher among them who was teaching it placed his palm on The verse of stoning, so he began to recite what was below his hand and what was behind it. He did not recite the verse of stoning, so Abdullah bin Salam struck his hand and said: What is this? He said: The verse about stoning. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to be stoned near where the funerals are placed. Abdullah said: So I saw. Its owner bends over it to protect it from the stones. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6941","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Al Jazari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “stoned a Jew, male and female, to the ground.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6942","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Harrani told me, he said: Ishaq bin Issa told us, he said: I am a partner, and another mentioned: Muhammad bin Jabir, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “stoned a Jew, male and female.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6943","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murrah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, who said: A flogged Jew passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he called them and said: “Is this how you find the punishment for the adulterer in your book?” They said: Yes, so he called a man from their scholars and said: I adjure you by God, do you find the punishment for the adulterer in your book? He said: No, and had you not asked me what? I'm right, we find it stoning, but it was common among our nobles. If we took the noble, we would leave him alone, and if the weak committed adultery, we would impose the punishment on him, so we said: Let us come together to agree on something that we can assess between the honorable and the lowly among us. So we agreed on bathing and flogging in the place of stoning, so God Almighty revealed: O Messenger, do not be saddened by those who hasten in disbelief to say: If you are given this, then take it. They say: Go to Muhammad, and if he gives you a fatwa By bathing and flogging, then take him, and if he gives you a fatwa of stoning, beware, to his saying: And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed Those are the disbelievers. He said regarding the Jews, up to His saying: And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed, those are the wrongdoers. He said regarding The Jews, to his saying: And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed - those are the transgressors. He said: It is among the disbelievers in all of them. The Messenger of God said. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O God, I am the first to revive Your command when they killed him.” So he ordered that he be stoned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6944","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: Ubay told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, he said: I am Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Abrogation of this Surah, meaning, two verses: the verse of the chains, and its saying: If they come to you, judge. between them or turn away from them, return them to their judges, until it was revealed: And to judge between them according to what God has revealed. He said: “Then the Messenger of God was commanded God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to judge between them according to what God has revealed.”"
"6945","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Zubaid, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahm, on the authority of Al-Baraa, that he mentioned a word, which means: “I I would go around those neighborhoods on my camels that had strayed during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a group of people came with them as their banner, and the Bedouins made They were seeking refuge with me because of my status with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so they extracted a man and beheaded him. I asked about his story, and they said: He married his father's wife (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6946","Yahya bin Hakim Al-Basri told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa, said: People passed by us as they were setting off, so we said to them: Where do you want? They said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent us “to a man who has intercourse with his father’s wife, to kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6947","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, told us, on the authority of Al-Sadi, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa, said: I met my uncle and he had the flag, so I said: Where do you want? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to: a man who married his father’s wife after him, to behead him or kill him. \"" 6948"""""
"6948","Muhammad ibn Rafi' informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara', from his father, who said: ""My uncle met me, and with him was the banner. I said: 'Where are you headed?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and he commanded me to kill him.'"""""
"6949","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Yusuf bin Manazil told us, he said: Abdullah bin Idris told us, he said: Khaled bin Abi Karimah told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah, on the authority of his father, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sent his father, Muawiyah’s grandfather, to a man who had married his father’s wife, So he beheaded him and took a fifth of his money. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6950","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abi Bishr, on the authority of Khalid bin Arafat, on the authority of Habib bin Salem On the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding a man having intercourse with his wife’s concubine, he said: “If she is permissible for him, “I will give him one hundred lashes, and if it is not permissible for him, I will stone him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6951","Yaqoub bin Mahan Al-Baghdadi told us, on the authority of Hushaym, who said: I am Abu Bishr, on the authority of Habib bin Salim, who said: A woman came to Al-Numan bin Bashir, and she said: Her husband had intercourse with her maid, so Al-Numan said: But I have satisfactory news about that, which I took from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you permit him, I will strike him one hundred times, and if you do not permit him, I will stone him.”"
"6952","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani told us, he said: Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl: She made it lawful for him, flog him with a hundred lashes, but if she did not make it lawful for him, then stone him.”"
"6953","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Khalid bin `Urfatah, on the authority of Habib ibn Salim, on the authority of al-Nu`man ibn Bashir, that a man called Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunayn used to go to Qarqura. And that he had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl, so it was brought to Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, and he said: I will decide for you according to the case of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If she made it permissible for you, I will lash you a hundred times, and if she did not make it permissible for you, I will stone you with stones.” He said: So she made it permissible for him, so he gave him a hundred lashes. Qatada said: So I wrote to Habib bin Salim, and he wrote to me with this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6954","Muhammad bin Muammar told me, he said: Habban told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatadah was asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl, so he told us and we Sitting, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Habib bin Yasaf, that it was presented to Al-Numan bin Bashir, and he said: I will judge it according to the judgment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: “If it is permissible for him, I will flog him a hundred times, and if it is not permissible for him, I will stone him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6955","Hannad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abdul Salam, who is Ibn Harb. He said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Mubaqq, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “A man who had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl was brought before him, but he did not challenge him.”"
"6956","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Muhabbiq, that a man went out in a raid He had with him a maidservant of his wife, and he had sexual intercourse with her. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If he forced her, then she is free. And he owes her the same, and if she obeys him, then she is a slave, and he owes the same for her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6957","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Muhabbiq said that a man had cheated on his wife’s slave girl, so the matter was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If He forced her, so she is free from his money, and he must give her money to her mistress, and if she obeyed him, then she is free from his money, and a similar share of his money. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6958","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Qubaisa ibn Harith On the authority of Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl, “If he forced her, then she is free.” And according to him, her mistress is entitled to the same, and if she obeyed him, then she is his, and according to him, her mistress is entitled to the same.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: There is nothing sound in this matter that can be used as evidence. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6959","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told us, he said: Abdul-Rahman is Ibn Mahdi told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz bin told us. Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, “orders that whoever commits adultery and is not married, one hundred lashes, and a year’s exile.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6960","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told him that Zayd bin Khalid Al-Juhani said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordering whom He was not chastised, with one hundred lashes, and a year of exile.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6961","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, he said: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd. By God, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled Al-Juhani, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He ordered that whoever commits adultery among an unmarried person should be flogged a hundred times.” “And a general exile.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6962","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, he said: Hujayn told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “decided that he who committed adultery and was not married should be exiled for a year, with the punishment being imposed on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6963","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Uwais told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, On the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle, who witnessed Badr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a female slave commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is for a braid.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Uwais is weak, and his son Ismail is weaker than him."
"6964","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Maysarah, on the authority of Ali, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Establish the limits on what your right hands possess.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6965","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Muawiyah told us that he is Ibn Hisham, he said: Sufyan told us that he is Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Habib, On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6966","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If the female slave of any of you commits adultery, let him flog her. If she commits adultery, let him flog her. If she commits adultery, Let him flog her, and if she commits adultery, let him sell her, even if it is for a strand of hair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6967","Othman bin Abdullah, who is Ibn Kharzaz, told me, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, he said: Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If she commits adultery with the servant of one of you, Let him flog her, he said, three times, and if she returns, let him sell her, even if it is for a strand of hair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6968","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If the female slave of any of you commits adultery, let him flog her according to the Book of God, and if she does so again, let him sell her, even if it is with a rope of \poetry\"""""""
"6969","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6970","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he heard him say: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, and her adultery becomes clear, let the punishment flog her, and not rebuke her, then “She commits adultery, then let the punishment flog her and not rebuke her, but if she commits the third adultery and her adultery becomes clear, then let him sell her, even if it is for a strand of hair.”"
"6971","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her, and do not rebuke her; but if she commits adultery, let him flog her. She committed adultery, so let him sell her, even if it is for a rope of hair or a braid of hair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6972","Qutaibah bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, and the wording is for Muhammad. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa, On the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, and her adultery becomes clear, Let the punishment flog her, but not flog her, three times.” Qutaibah added: “And if she commits adultery, let him sell her, even if it is for a braid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6973","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Hisham is Ibn Hassan told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; if she commits adultery, let him flog her.” And he should not rebuke her, but if she commits adultery, he should sell her, even if it is for a braid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6974","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace be upon him, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her and not rebuke her, then if she commits adultery, let him flog her and not rebuke her, then if she commits adultery, let him flog her and not rebuke her.” She committed adultery, so let him sell her, even if it is for a strand of hair.” Ali bin Saeed bin Jarir Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. . . So on (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6975","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Bishr, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, And Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, speaking on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If a female slave commits adultery, flog her, and do not rebuke her, and then She commits adultery, flog her and do not rebuke her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her and do not rebuke her. Then sell her for the third or fourth time, then Sell it, even if it is for a bit.” Bishr said in his hadith: “Then if she commits adultery, flog her, and do not rebuke her, then sell her, even if it is only for a rope.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6976","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Ismail bin Umayyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the female slave of one of you commits adultery, and her adultery becomes clear, then he should flog her, and not punish her.” And if she commits adultery again, let him flog her, and not rebuke her. If she commits adultery again, let him sell her, even if it is for a strand of hair.”"
"6977","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me. He said: Abu al-Jawab, who is Al-Ahwas bin Jawab, told us. He said: Ammar, who is Ibn Ruzaiq, told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My maid committed adultery, and her adultery became clear. He said: Flog her fifty, then he came to him and said: She returned and her adultery became clear. He said: Give her fifty lashes. Then he came to him and said: She returned and her adultery became clear. He said: Sell her, even if it is for a strand of hair. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6978","Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa, who is Ibn Ayn al-Jazari, narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Ishaq Bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a man came to him, He said: “My daughter committed adultery.” He said: “Give her fifty lashes.” He said: “And if she repeats it?” He said: “Then return.” He said: “And if she does commit adultery?” He said: “Then return.” Then, if she returns. So sell it, even if it is for a braid,” in the fourth or third, and the braid: the rope. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an error, the one before it is an error, and the one before it is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6979","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ayyub told us, he is ibn Sulaiman ibn Bilal, he said: Abu Bakr told me, he is ibn Abi Uwais. On the authority of Suleiman, he is Ibn Bilal. He said: Yahya said he is Ibn Sa’id, and Ibn Shihab told me that Ubayd Allah Ibn Abdullah, He told him that Abu Hurairah and Zaid bin Khalid told him that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, being asked about the nation if She committed adultery and was not married? He said: “Flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is with a braid.” After the third or fourth, and the braid: the rope. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6980","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, He told him that Abu Hurairah and Zayd bin Khalid told him that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, being asked about the nation. She commits adultery and is not married. He said: “Flog her if she commits adultery, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is for a braid.” “After the third, or the fourth"
"6981","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zayd bin Khaled, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a female slave who committed adultery and was not married? He said: “If she commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is for a braid.” After the third Or the fourth, and the braid: the rope."
"6982","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu A kitten and a young lion. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a female slave who committed adultery before she was married. He said: “Flog her. If she commits adultery, So flog her.” And he said: On the fourth or third: “Sell it, even if it is for a plait.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The correct hadith is the hadith of Malik, and Shibl in this hadith is an error. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6983","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubaid Allah informed me Bin Abdullah, that Shibl bin Khalid Al-Muzani told him that Abdullah bin Malik Al-Awsi told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If the female child commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. “So flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is for a braid.” The braid: the rope, in the third or fourth strand. Zaid bin Khalid told him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Like that"
"6984","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My nephew Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of his uncle Muhammad bin Muslim, he said: Ubaid Allah bin told me Abdullah, that Shibl bin Hamid Al-Muzani, told him that Abdullah bin Malik Al-Awsi, told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him He greeted him and said: “If the female child commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, flog her. Then if she commits adultery, sell her, even if it is for a braid.” The braid: the rope, in the third or fourth strand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6985","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa ibn Bahloul al-Homsi informed us, saying: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah Shibl bin Khalid Al-Muzani told him that Abdullah bin Malik Al-Awsi told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “If the female child commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, then sell her, even if With a braid.” The braid: the rope (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6986","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman, the companion of Al-Shafi’i, told me, he said: Shuaib told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Farwah, that Muhammad bin Muslim narrated it, that Urwa bin Al-Zubayr narrated it, that Amra bint Abdul Rahman narrated it, that Aisha I told her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a female slave commits adultery, flog her; So flog her, then sell her, even if it is for a fee.” The braid: the rope (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6987","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Farwa, that Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to him, That Urwa and Amra told him, that Aisha told them, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a female slave commits adultery, Then flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is for a braid.” The braid: the rope (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6988","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If the mukatib attains a punishment, or an inheritance, and he inherits on the basis of what he has freed, The punishment was imposed on him on account of what was freed from him.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is not correct, and there is disagreement about it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6989","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, who is Al-Thaalabi, On the authority of Abu Jamila, on the authority of Ali, he said: A maid of mine committed adultery, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Do not hit her until she gives birth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6990","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, he said: Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Abu Jamila, on the authority of Ali, that a nation She committed adultery to the Prophet, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perform punishment upon her.” I looked, and the blood had not dried from her, so I came to the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: When the blood dries up from her, and establish boundaries over what your right hands possess. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6991","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Jamila, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed Peace be upon him and greeted a nation of theirs that had committed adultery, so he sent me to her and said: “Go and perform the punishment upon her.” So I set off and found that she had not dried up. of her blood, so I returned to him and said to him: I found that her blood had not dried up, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So, she Her blood dried, so he flogged her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Establish punishments over what your right hands possess.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abd al-Ala is not that strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6992","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a prostituted woman who was in childbirth, to restrain her. He said: “Go until the blood stops from you.” He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman: This is an objectionable hadith and nothing."
"6993","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala Kufi informed us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father He said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Ghamidiyah from Al-Azd came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I committed adultery. He sent her back, and she said: O Messenger of God, do you want to return me as you returned a goat? By God, I am now pregnant. He said: Go until you give birth. Then she came and said: You have given birth, O Messenger of God. He said: Go until you give birth. Wean him, so she weaned him, then she brought him with a piece of bread in his hand to eat, and she said: I have weaned him, and now he is eating, so the Messenger pushed him away. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to a man from among the Muslims, then he ordered them to dig a hole for her up to her chest, then he ordered his companions to stone her. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid threw a stone at her, and some of her blood spilled on Khaled’s forehead. He cursed her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: And he said hello: Curs her, Khaled. She has repented with such a repentance that if the owner of a tax had repented, God would have repented of him, then he commanded that she be shrouded, then he prayed over her.” Bashir said. Ibn Buraydah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: We were the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, talking about a goat and this woman. They did not answer on the fourth day. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not ask them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6994","Yaqoub bin Sufyan Al-Farisi told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told me, he said: Al-Qasim bin Rushdin bin Umair told me, he said: Makhramah bin Bukair told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, that he heard Al-Sharid, who is Ibn Suwayd, say: A woman was stoned for... The time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When we had finished with it, I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: We have stoned this woman. Evil, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Stoning is an expiation for what you have done.” Ibn Wahb disagreed with him."
"6995","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Hibb informed me, saying: Makhramah informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Sharid, he said: A woman was stoned to stone during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so when we finished with her, I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, So I said: O Messenger of God, we have stoned this evil woman, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is the expiation for what she has done.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Amr ibn al-Sharid has no companions, and al-Qasim ibn Rishdin, I do not know him, and he seems to be a civilian. And Makhramah bin Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, he did not hear from his father. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6996","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Yazid bin Nu’aym, on the authority of his father, That Ma'iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Perform the Book of God upon me. He turned away from it four times, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered He was stoned, and when the stones touched him, he went out in distress, and Abdullah bin Unais left his people’s camp with the back of a donkey. He struck him and knocked him down. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and spoke to him. He ordered him and said: “Don’t you leave him alone? Perhaps he will repent, so God will repent.” On it, then he said: O Hazal, if you covered him with your dress, it would be better for you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6997","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir. On the authority of Ibn Hazal, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woe to you, O Hazal. If you covered him with your garment, it would be better.” \For you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6998","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: I am Abdullah and he is Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Muhammad ibn What is unfortunate is that a man named Huzal was the one who advised him to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him He said: “O Hazzal, if you covered him with your dress, it would be better for you.” Yahya said: So I mentioned this hadith to his son’s son, Yazid bin Nu’aym bin Hazzal, and he said: He is my grandfather. He said: This was (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6999","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to a man who converted to Islam, called Huzal: “O Huzal, if you covered him with your cloak, It would be better for you.” Yahya said: This hadith was narrated in a gathering in which Yazid ibn Nu`aym ibn Hazal al-Aslami was present, and Yazid said: Hazal is serious, and this The hadith is true"
"7000","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Yazid bin Nu’aym, on the authority of his grandfather Hazzal, that it was a matter of goats. That he would come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and tell him his hadith. Then a goat came and told him, so he turned away from it, and he was repeating that. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he sent to his people and asked them: “Is he mad? They said: No, so he asked about him: Is he a virgin or a virgin?” They said: Thayb, so he ordered that he be stoned, then he said: O Hazal, if you had covered him, it would have been better for you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7001","Muhammad bin Miskin told us in Basra, he said: Ubadah bin Omar told us, he said: Ikrimah, who is Ibn Ammar told us, he said: I heard Yazid bin Nu’aym bin Hazal, on the authority of his father, that Hazal told him that Ma’iz, who was a relative of Hazal, happened upon a relative of Hazal, and that He was still emaciated with a goat, ordering him to confess and repent, until he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded upon him and grant him peace by stoning him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7002","Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Basri told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abu Salamah bin told me. Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Yazid bin Nu`aym bin Hazzal, who was Hazzal and used to shed goats, who said: My family had a maid who took care of sheep for them. It is said to her: Fatima, she has become king, and that a goat fell on her, and that an emaciated goat took it, and said to it: Go to the Prophet, may God bless him. And peace be upon him, so we will tell him what you have done, in the hope that the Qur’an will be revealed to you. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered it to be done, so he was stoned, but when she bit him, he touched it. stones, he set off, and a man met him with such-and-such, or a camel’s leg, and he hit him, knocking him down, and said: “Oh Hazzal, if you had covered him With your clothes, it will be better for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7003","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nashit, on the authority of Ka’b bin Alqamah, that Uqba bin Amir, said : I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever sees a private part and covers it, it is as if he revived a dead woman from her grave.”"
"7004","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb, and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, in his hadith on the authority of Ibn Wahb, He said: Ibrahim bin Nushait informed me, on the authority of Ka’b bin Alqamah, on the authority of Kathir, the client of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sees a private part and covers it, it is as if he who saw a woman returning to life from her grave was ashamed.”"
"7005","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Nushait told us, on the authority of Ka’b bin Alqamah, He said: I heard Abu Al-Haytham mentioning that he heard Dakhin, the clerk of Aqaba, say: We had neighbors who drank alcohol, so I forbade them, but they did not They finished, so I said to Uqba bin Amir: They are drinking alcohol, and I forbade them, but they did not stop, so call for the condition for them? He said: No, then I went back to him, and he said: Leave them, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever sees the private parts of a Muslim, So he covered her, and it was as if she was alive and loving.”"
"7006","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahwi told us, and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Hisham. He is Ibn Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Wasi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Who will cover His Muslim brother in this world, God will protect him in this world and the hereafter, and whoever relieves his brother of the distress of this world, God will relieve him. A distress of the distress of the Day of Resurrection, and God will help the servant, as long as the servant helps his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7007","Ahmad ibn al-Khalil al-Naysaburi, whose origin is Baghdadi, narrated to us. He said: We have a soul, and he is Ibn Ubadah. He said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Wasi’, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever relieves Whoever protects his Muslim brother, God will relieve him of the distress of the Hereafter, and whoever protects his Muslim brother, God will protect him in this world. And in the Hereafter, God helps the servant, as long as the servant helps his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7008","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, and he is bin Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, he said: A man told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever relieves a Muslim of the distress of this world, God will relieve him.” distress from the distress of the Hereafter, and whoever protects his believing brother in this world, God will protect him in the Hereafter, and God helps the servant, so long as the servant is in \help his brother\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7009","Al-Abbas bin Abdullah bin Abbas Al-Antaki told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aisha told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever relieves His brother is in distress, may God relieve him of distress on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever protects his Muslim brother, God will protect him in this world. And in the Hereafter, by God, He is in the need of the servant, as the servant is not in the need of his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7010","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever relieves a Muslim of the distress of this world, God will relieve him of the distress of the Hereafter, and whoever covers a Muslim, God will protect him in this world and the hereafter, and God helps the servant, as long as the servant helps his brother.” Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Al-Numan told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, And perhaps he said: On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever relieves a Muslim’s distress. . . , just like him. Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samurah al-Kufi told me, he said: Asbat narrated to us, he is the son of Muhammad. He said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, he said: I narrated on the authority of my father. Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7011","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. He does not wrong him or betray him. Whoever is in the need of his brother, God will be in his need. And whoever relieves a Muslim of distress, God will relieve him of distress on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever protects a Muslim, God will relieve him of distress on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"7012","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, he said: We were He was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a gathering, and said: “You pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with God, and you do not steal, and you do not commit adultery.” He read to them. The verse: So whoever of you fulfills his duty, his reward is with God, and whoever does any of this afflicts him, God will cover him for it. It is to God. If He wills, He will punish him. And if He wills, He will forgive him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7013","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Attaf bin Khalid told us, he said: Abdul told me Al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “Dismiss those who are in good standing because of their offenses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7014","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Zayd al-Madani told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Remove those who are of poor appearance, except for the punishments.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7015","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: I am Suwayd, he is Ibn Nasr, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “They overlooked a mistake.” \the one with the form\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7016","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Abdullah bin Maslamah bin Qanab told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They were dismissed.” Those with bad appearances are stumbling blocks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7017","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Ibn Abi Al-Rijal told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abdul Al-Aziz bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al-Khattab said: A master of mine whom I wounded attacked me. It is said to him: Greetings of the Barbarian, to Ibn Hazm. He said: Did you hurt him? I said: Yes, and he said: I heard from my aunt Amra, saying: Aisha said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Remove those with bad appearances.” I stumbled upon them.” He said: So he let him go, and did not punish him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7018","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told me, he said: Ma’an told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr. Ibn Amr Ibn Hazm, on the authority of Amra, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Remove those of bad appearance because of their offenses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7019","Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Naysaburi informed us. He said: I am Muhammad ibn Sulaiman. He said: Ubayd Allah told us. Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Yazid informed us. Ibn Ibrahim Al-Harrani, he said: Abi told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaid, he is the son of Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought to a man who had committed adultery. He ordered him to be stripped, and then there was a paralyzed man with his legs crossed. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Nothing of this will remain from being struck.” So he called for a basket containing a hundred shamrocks, and struck him with it. One hit. The word is for Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7020","Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Zaid told me, on the authority of Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abi Umamah bin Sahl, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a slave girl who was pregnant, and it was said to her: Who Do I love you? She said: So-and-so is paralyzed. Then so-and-so was brought, and behold, there was a man with a broken body, blind, and he said: “By God, the beating of this man will not cause any harm.” So he ordered With hundred weights of weight, they were gathered together, and he was struck with them with one plague.” These are the palm trees from which the stems are (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7021","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah is Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, he said: I am Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abu Umamah Ibn Sahl, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought to a seat that was at Sa’d’s wall. He confessed and said: “Flog him with the weight of palm trees.” \. It means the roots of palm trees (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"7022","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri informed us. Sufyan said: We preserved it from Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa’id, that he heard Abu Umamah, he says: There was a man at Saad’s wall who had been sitting for some time, when a pregnancy appeared to his wife, and she said: It is from him. He was asked, so he confessed, so he commanded. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “To be flogged with the weight of palm trees.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7023","Muhammad ibn Mansour informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: We preserved it from Abu al-Zinad, and Yahya ibn Sa`id, they heard it from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl bin Hunaif, that Ajirab Aziman was at Saad’s wall and committed adultery with a woman. “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered that he be flogged.” One of them said: “With fronds of palm trees,” and the other said: “With froths of palm trees.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7024","Yaqoub bin Mahan Al-Baghdadi informed us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he greeted, “A man was brought who was insane, or paralyzed, and had broken his fast. An order was given to him, and he was struck with weights containing a hundred spears,” or something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7025","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth told me, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed said that Abu Umamah bin Sahl told him that a man had committed adultery during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and committed adultery. Then he was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and it was said to him: O Messenger of God, if you flog him, you will kill him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Strike him with heavy weights of palm trees,” and he was struck with it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7026","Muhammad ibn Jablah al-Rafiqi told me, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah, He said: A man among them fell ill until he became skin on bones, then a maid who was accustomed to him came in and he fell upon her and was heartbroken by his sin, so he said For a people who use it as a habit: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for me, for I have committed an unlawful act with a woman, so let him carry out the punishment on me and purify me. So they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then they said: If he were brought to you, his bones would rot, and if he were struck, he would die. So he said: “Take a hundred shamrocks and strike him with them once.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7027","Muhammad bin Jabla told me, he said: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib told me, he said: Musa told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Sahl ibn Hunaif, who said: A man became ill until he recovered skin on bones, then a maid came in to visit him, and he fell on her. He became distressed by his sin, so he said to the people who were visiting him: Ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for me, for I have committed an unlawful act with a woman. Let the punishment be imposed on me and purify me. They mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then they said: If he were brought to you, his bones would rot. If he had been struck by a hundred, he would have died. He said: “Take a hundred shamrocks and strike them once.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7028","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, On the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Sa’d, he said: There was among our descendants a man who was physically blind, and he did not take care of the people of the house except when he was That is, a girl from the neighborhood of the house, with whom debauchery was committed. So Saad reported his matter to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Strike him severely. They said: O Messenger of God, if we strike him we will kill him. He is weaker than that. He said: Take a stick from it.” A hundred spears, strike him with one blow.” So they did. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7029","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj told me, on the authority of my father Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif said that a woman became pregnant, and she was asked: From whom? She said: From so-and-so who was crippled and weak. He was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was questioned and he confessed and said: “Strike him.” They said: We are afraid. To die, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Strike him with burdens.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7030","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Harrani informed us, saying: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talha, who is al-Qannad, told us, on the authority of Asbat ibn Nasr, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Alqama bin Wael, on the authority of his father, claimed that a man had sexual intercourse on a woman in the dark of the morning while she was going to the mosque wearing perfume. Forced upon herself, she sought help from a man who passed by her, and her companion fled, then a number of people passed by her, so she sought help from them, and they overtook her. The man whom she had sought for help, so they took him, and the other one preceded them, so they brought him and led him to her, and he said to her: I am the one who helped you. The other one went away and said: They brought him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she told him that he had intercourse with her, and he told the people that they They found him getting hard, so he said: I was helping it to its owner, but these people overtook me and took me. She said: He lied, he was the one who attacked me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go with him and stone him.” Then a man from among the people stood up and said: “Do not stone him, but stone me, for I will The one who did the deed to her, so he confessed, and three gathered with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the one who had a sexual intercourse with her, and the one who helped her. And the woman, so he said: As for you, you have been forgiven, and he said a good word to the one who helped her, so Omar said: Should the one who confessed to adultery be stoned, but he refused? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No, he has repented to God.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The best of them is the hadith of Abu Umamah, mursal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7031","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, he said: Shaddad Abu Ammar told me, that Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ told him He said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have injured someone, so set him on me, so the Messenger of God turned away from him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the prayer was established. When he said the salutation, he said: O Messenger of God, I have injured someone, so make him my master. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Did you perform ablution when you came? He said: Yes, he said: Did you pray with us? He said: Yes, he said: Then go, for God has pardoned.” “About you.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: We do not know that anyone followed Al-Walid on what he said, on the authority of Wathilah, and the correct thing is: Abu Ammar, on the authority of Abu Umamah, And God knows best"
"7032","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Omar told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Abu Ammar told me, he said: Abu Umamah told me, that a man, He said: O Messenger of God, I have injured someone, so appoint him to me. He said: Did you perform ablution when you came? He said: Yes. He said: Did you pray with us? He said: Yes, he said: So go, for God has pardoned you."
"7033","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, he said: My father told me, he said: I am Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Ammar, a man from among us, told me, on the authority of my father Umamah, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: I have struck a punishment, so appoint him to me, and the prayer was established. When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, greeted May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, I have injured someone, so appoint him to me. He said: Did you perform ablution when you came? He said: Yes. He said: Go, for God has pardoned you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7034","Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Abu Ammar Shaddad told me, he said: Abu Umamah told me, That a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have injured someone, so appoint him over me, so he turned away from him, then he said: I I struck a punishment, so he made him stand over me, and he turned away from him. Then he said: O Messenger of God, I struck a punishment, so he turned away from him, and the prayer was established, so when The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him. He said: O Messenger of God, I have encountered a punishment, so appoint him to me. He said: Did you perform ablution when you came? He said: Yes. He said: Did you pray with us when we prayed? He said: Yes. He said: “Go, for God has pardoned you.”"
"7035","Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq Al-Kufi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, he said: Abu Ammar Shaddad bin Abdullah, he said: Abu Umamah told me, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I have fulfilled one of the punishments of God. So he made him lead me, and he remained silent, then he repeated it, and he remained silent, then the prayer was performed, and he prayed, then he left, and a man followed him, and he repeated it. He said: “Did you perform ablution well when you left your house, and then prayed with us?” He said: Yes. He said: Indeed, God has forgiven you. Your sin, or your punishment.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7036","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb and al-A’mash, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Oh Messenger of God, I have suffered from everything from it, except intercourse, so God Almighty revealed: And establish prayer at two ends of the day (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7037","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told me, he said: Al-Sinani told us, and his name is Al-Fadl bin Musa Abu Abdullah, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Messenger of By God, I had been afflicted by a woman, but I had not had intercourse with her. So God Almighty revealed: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7038","Ahmad bin Sufyan Al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Saeed bin Al-Rabi’, who is Abu Zaid Al-Harawi, narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of my uncle, on the authority of Abdullah, said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I struck a woman in a room of Hashush Al-Madinah, so I had some of them other than intercourse, so this verse was revealed: “And perform prayer at both ends of the day.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Haytham Abu Qatn told me, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ibrahim. On the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7039","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Abdullah told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of his uncle. Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, said that a man met a woman on one of the roads of Medina, and had sexual intercourse with her, short of sexual intercourse, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so that was mentioned to him, so God Almighty revealed regarding that: And establish prayer at both ends of the day and at the end of the night: for those who remember. Muadh said: O Messenger of God, did it come down specifically for this purpose, or for us in general? He said: “Rather, for you in general.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7040","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Amr bin Hammad told us, he said: Asbat told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abd. God, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, I took a woman in the gardens, and I did everything to her. Nothing, except that I did not see anything forbidden from her, so I kissed her and committed to her, and I did not do anything else, so do with me whatever you want. No messenger said to him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked something, so the man went, and Omar said: God has covered this. If only he had covered himself, the Messenger of God followed him. A man, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He returned it to me, so he came and recited to him: And perform prayer at the two ends of the day.” Muadh said: Is this the case or is it? For people in general, O Prophet of God? He said: For people in general. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7041","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I took a woman in the garden, and I was fine with everything, except that I did not marry her. So do with me whatever you want. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not say anything to him. Then he called him and recited to him this verse: And perform the prayer. At the end of the day and at the end of the night, indeed, good deeds remove bad deeds. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7042","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Al-Aswad. Ibn Masoud said: He came A man, and he said: I treated a woman in the furthest part of the city, and I was infected with her without even touching her. Then Omar said: God has forsaken you, if only You covered yourself, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not reply anything, so he got up and went off, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed him, and a man called him. When he came to him, he recited to him: “And perform prayer at both ends of the day” for “those who remember,” and a man from among the people said: This is for him, O Prophet of God, in particular? He said: “Rather, for all people.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The Messenger is more likely to be correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7043","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, It was said to him: So-and-so bin Mu’tab, and he said: “O Messenger of God, I went in to a woman and got from her what a man gets from his family, except that I did not Its timing, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not know what to answer him, until this verse was revealed to him: And perform prayer at two ends of the day and walk away. From the night, the verse, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and recited it to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7044","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said that a man had received a kiss from a woman, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned that to him, so God revealed: And stand. Prayer is the two ends of the day. The man said: What is this for, O Messenger of God? He said: “Rather, it is for those of my nation who act upon it.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7045","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: I am Suwayd, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sharik, he said: Uthman bin Mawhib told us, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr said: “I came to a woman, and her husband had been sent by the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a mission, and she said to him: Sell me for a dirham.” Dates, so I said to her, and I liked them: There are better dates in the house than these, so he went off with them, winked at her, and kissed her, and he finished, then He went out and met Abu Bakr, and said to him: I have perished. He said to him: What is the matter with you? So he told him his story, and said to him: Is there any repentance for me? He said: Yes, repent, and do not repeat it, and do not tell anyone. Then he set off until he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him his story, and said: You left a man behind. Who among the Muslims is fighting for the sake of God in this way? So I thought that I was one of the people of Hell, and that God would never forgive me, and the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, departed from me. May God bless him and grant him peace, until it was revealed to him: And perform prayer at both ends of the day as a remembrance for those who remember. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to me He said hello, and he recited them to me (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7046","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, that a man came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I have had sexual intercourse with a woman without intercourse, so God revealed this verse: And perform prayer at two ends of the day. And towards the end of the night, he went to: a remembrance for those who remember, and Muadh said: O Messenger of God, is it a special one for him? He said: “Rather, for all people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7047","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Huraym bin Sufyan told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays, On the authority of Abu Shahm, he said: “I was in Medina, and a maid passed by me, so I took her handbag, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was He pledged allegiance to people. He said: Aren’t you the owner of the cake? I said: O Messenger of God, I will not return. So he pledged allegiance to me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7048","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Fulan, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Nayyar, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He shall not be subjected to more than ten lashes, other than the limits set by God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7049","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Niyar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not flog me.” More than ten lashes, except within the limits set by God.”"
"7050","Muhammad bin Wahb told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahim, he said: Zayd bin Abi Unaisa told me, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukayr Ibn Abdullah, who said: While I was with Suleiman, Abd al-Rahman Ibn Jabir came and spoke to Suleiman, then Suleiman approached them and said: Abd al-Rahman bin Jabir told me that his father told him that he heard Abu Burdah al-Ansari say: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no flogging for more than ten lashes, except within the limits set by God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7051",": On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’, on the authority of Fudayl bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jabir, on the authority of He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “He shall not be flogged more than ten lashes, except within the limits set by God.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jaber, no problem (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7052","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Sa’d said: “O Messenger of God, What do you think, if I find a man with my wife, should I give him time until I bring four witnesses? He said: Yes?"
"7053","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Jews came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they mentioned to him that a man and a woman had committed adultery, so he said to them: “What do you find in the Torah regarding stoning?” So they said: We expose them. And they will be flogged. Abdullah bin Salam said: It includes stoning. So they brought the Torah, and one of them put his hand on the verse about stoning and recited what came before it. And after that, Abdullah bin Salam said to him: Raise your hand, so he raised his hand, and when it contained the verse of stoning, they said: You are right, Muhammad. It contains a verse about stoning. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to be stoned. Abdullah bin Omar said: I saw the man leaning toward the woman. He protects it from stones (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7054","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: He mentioned cursing in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Asim bin Adi said something about that, then he left, Then a man from his people came to him, complaining to him that he had found a man with his family. Asim said: I was not afflicted with this except by what I said, so he took him away. to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he informed him of what he found his wife with, and that man was yellow-haired, of little meat, and short-skinned. The one who claimed that he had found a sheep with a lot of flesh among his family, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh God, make clear. Then she placed something similar to the man whom her husband mentioned that he found next to her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed between them.” He said A man told Ibn Abbas in the council: Is she the one whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If I stoned anyone without proof, I would stone this woman”? Ibn Abbas said: No, that is a woman who used to show evil in Islam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7055","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He mentioned those who curse, and Abdullah bin Shaddad said: Is she the woman whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If I were a stoner without Clearly, I stoned her? He said: No, that is a woman who announced (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7056","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is Al-Darawardi, told us, on the authority of Amr, who is Ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse whoever does the actions of the people of Lot. May God curse whoever does the actions of the people of Lot. May God curse whoever does the actions of the people of Lot.”"
"7057","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr and Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “In the case of a virgin, he is found guilty of sodomy. He said: He will be stoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7058","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “May God curse whoever falls on an animal.”"
"7059","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever you find has fallen upon an animal, kill him and kill the animal.” Then it was said to Ibn Abbas: What is the matter with the animal? He said: I did not hear anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, but I see that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hated being eaten by food. Its flesh, or to benefit from it, and that work was done with it."
"7060","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-Numan, meaning Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Asim, who is Ibn Bahdala, on the authority of Abu Razin, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, he said: “There is no punishment for whoever has sex with an animal.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is not known, and the first is the preserved one."
"7061","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He struck and went astray,” and that Abu Bakr struck and went astray, and that Omar struck and went astray. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7062","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, in his hadith, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Jarir bin Hazim informed me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mahran, On the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by an insane woman from the tribe of so-and-so who had committed adultery, so Omar ordered her to be stoned. Ali bin Abi Talib returned it and said to Omar: O Commander of the Faithful, you have ordered that this woman be stoned! ! He said: Yes, he said: And do you remember that the Messenger of God said: “The pen was lifted from three: from the insane who lost his mind, and from the sleeper until He wakes up, and about the boy until he dreams? He said: You are right. He said: So he left her."
"7063","Hilal bin Bishr told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Samad told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, he said: Omar had a woman brought to him. She had committed adultery and had her child with her, so he ordered her to be stoned. Then Ali passed by and sent her away, and said: This is the affliction of the children of so-and-so, then he said: By God, this has I learned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The pen has been lifted from three people: from the sleeper until he awakens, and from the afflicted person until he becomes sensible. And on behalf of the child until he reaches puberty, he grows up.”"
"7064","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ali, he said: “It was raised “The pen is for three things: for the sleeper until he wakes up, for the lunatic, and for the child.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more likely to be correct, and Abu Husayn is more reliable than Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib, and Jarir bin Hazim did not narrate it in Egypt. It is not that, and his hadith on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub as well, it is not that."
"7065","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The Pen was lifted from three people: from the sleeper until he awakens, and the insane person, or he said: the insane person until he becomes sensible, and the child until he grows old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7066","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The pen was lifted from three people: on the authority of the sleeper. “Until he wakes up, for a boy until he reaches the age of perjury, and for an insane person until what is wrong with him is revealed.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Nothing in it is correct, and what is given is more correct, this one is more likely to be correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7067","Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Musa bin Harun Al-Bardi told us, he said: Hisham bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Fayyad told us, on the authority of Khallad Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn al-Musayyib, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man from Banu Laith Ibn Bakr came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said, “So he admitted that he had committed adultery with a woman four times, so he gave him one hundred lashes, and he was a virgin, and he asked him for evidence about the woman, and she said The woman: He lied, by God, O Messenger of God, so he was given the skin of a libel, eighty.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7068","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Haywa bin Shurayh told me, on the authority of Salim bin Ghaylan al-Tajibi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yassar, that some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “flogged a man because he called another the son of a madman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7069","Ya'qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “If one of you strikes, let him avoid the face.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7070","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “When my excuse came down, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up on the pulpit. He mentioned that and recited. When he came down from the pulpit, He ordered the two men and the woman to be beaten.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7071","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Fudayl Ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of my father Hurairah said that he told him, he said: Abu Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the Prophet of Repentance, said: “Whoever slanders his slave is innocent of what he said, he will be held against him.” The punishment on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he said.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is a good hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7072","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Yazid is the son of Harun, he said: I am Sufyan, he is the son of Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: “Whoever slanders his slave, God will have a punishment for him on the Day of Resurrection. If He wishes, He can take it, and if He wishes, He can pardon him.”"
"7073","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Mihran, and Ahmad ibn Mihran informed us. Sayyar, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Muhammad said: On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not steal when he steals.” He is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks while he is a believer. Then repentance is offered afterward.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7074","7113 Abu Ali Muhammad bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Saleh On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he is a believer, nor does he drink alcohol while he is a believer. And he mentioned a fourth time and I forgot about it, so when he did that, he took off the tie of Islam from his neck, and if he repented, God would repent to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7075","7114 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, and Ahmad bin Harb, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “May God curse the thief who steals an egg and his hand is cut off, and he steals a rope and his hand is cut off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7076","7115 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Habib told me, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, “that a man stole A garment for herself, so she went to pray for it, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not make a slander on his behalf.” Abdul Rahman sent him, Muhammad ibn Bashar, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’, sent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7077","7117 Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Abu Usama told us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak told me, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “detained people on charges” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7078","Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imprisoned a man on an accusation, then released him.”"
"7079","7118 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Abu Al-Mundhir, the client of Abu Dhar, on the authority of Abu Umayyah Al-Makhzoumi, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with a thief who confessed. There was no belongings with him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: I do not think you have stolen. He said: Yes, he said: Go with it and cut it up, then? They took him and cut him off, then they brought him, and he said to him: Say, I ask forgiveness from God and repent to him. He said: I ask forgiveness from God and repent to him. He said: Oh God, repent. \on him\"""""""
"7080","7119 Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, “A man stole his cloak, so he took it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered that it be cut off, and he said: O Messenger of God.” I had left Abu Wahb with him. Was it not before you brought him? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke up with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7081","7120 Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Tariq ibn Murqa’, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, “A man stole his cloak, so he took it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: So he ordered it to be cut off. He said: O Messenger of God, I have neglected it. He said: Had this not happened before you brought it to me, O Abu? He gave a gift, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut it off.” Al-Awza’i disagreed with him, so he sent the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7082","7121 Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: he told me Ata bin Abi Rabah, “A man stole a garment, and it was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He ordered that it be cut, and the man said: Oh Messenger of God, it is his. He said: Welcome before now. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7083","7122 Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, he is the son of Abi Bashir, He said: Ikrimah told me, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, “He circumambulated the Kaaba and prayed, then he wrapped a cloak for himself and placed it under His head and he slept, then a thief came to him and took it from under his head and took it, and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This man had stolen My robe. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Did you steal this robe? He said: Yes. He said: Go with it. They cut off his hand. Safwan said: I did not want his hand to be cut off while on my cloak, so he said to him: If it had not happened before this, Ash’ath ibn Sawwar disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7084","7123 Muhammad bin Hisham told us, he said: Al-Fadl, meaning Ibn Al-Ala’ Al-Kufi, told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, he is Ibn Siwar, and he Da’eef, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “Safwan was sleeping in the mosque with his robe underneath him, and he was stolen, and he got up and went.” The man overtook him, took him, and brought him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered that it be cut. Safwan said: O Messenger of God, what has reached When a man was cut into my cloak, he said: Was this before you brought it to us? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7085","7124 Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told me, he said: Amr told us, on the authority of Asbat, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Humaid, the son of Safwan’s sister, On the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, he said: “I was sleeping in the mosque on a piece of clothing that cost me thirty dirhams, then a man came and stole it from me. So he took the man and brought him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to be cut off, so I came to him and said to him: Will you cut him off for thirty dirhams? I will sell it and give him its price. He said: Was this before you brought it to me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7086","7125 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Safwan ibn Umayyah, “His khamis was stolen from under his head while he was sleeping in a mosque.” The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took the thief and brought him to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He ordered that he be cut, and Safwan said: Will you cut him? He said: So, before you bring him to me, you left him alone. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7087","7126 Muhammad ibn Dawud told me, he said: We narrated to Mu’alla ibn Asad, he said: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah said: I said: O Messenger of God, this man stole a khamis of mine from a man who had it with him, so he ordered it to be cut off, so I said: O Messenger of God. I have given it to him. He said: So come before you bring it to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7088","7127 Muhammad bin Hashim told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Follow the limits between yourselves before you come to me, for whoever comes to me in any way, it is obligatory.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7089","7128 Al-Harith bin Miskin A reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: I heard Ibn Jurayj narrating, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be careful of the boundaries between yourselves, for no punishment has reached me.” \It is obligatory\"""""""
"7090","7129 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “A Makhzoumiya woman was borrowing belongings and would deny them, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her hand to be cut off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7091","7130 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of"
"7092","7131 Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Hammad told me, he said: Amr bin Hashim Al-Janabi Abu Malik told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “A woman used to borrow jewelry for people, then keep it, and the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Let this woman repent to God and His Messenger, and return what she has taken from the people. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said “Arise, O Bilal, and take her by the hand and cut it off.” Shuaib disagreed with him, so he sent the hadith."
"7093","7132 Muhammad ibn al-Khalil informed me, on the authority of Shuaib ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, “A woman was borrowing jewelry in At the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she borrowed some jewelry from that man and collected it, then she held it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “Let this woman repent to God and give what she owes.” He repeatedly said, but she did not do so, so He commanded her to do so, and she was cut off. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7094","7133 Muhammad ibn Ma’dan ibn Issa informed us, saying: He is the son of Muhammad ibn Ayan. Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Maqil ibn Ubaid narrated to us. God, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “A woman from Banu Makhzum stole, and she was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she sought refuge with a mother.” Salamah. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If it were Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, I would have cut off her hand, and her hand was cut off. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7095","7134 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, “A woman from Banu Makhzum borrowed some jewelry from someone, but they denied it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that it be given away.” So it was cut off. “Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, that Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrated to him, something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
